To turn this mock-up into an interactive website with a real joke, you can use HTML and JavaScript. Here's a simple example:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>My Joke Website</title>
    <style>
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            display: flex;
            justify-content: center;
            align-items: center;
            height: 100vh;
            background-color: #f0f0f0;
        }
        .container {
            border: 2px solid #333;
            padding: 20px;
            border-radius: 10px;
            background-color: #fff;
            box-shadow: 0 0 10px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);
        }
        h1 {
            color: #333;
        }
        .joke {
            margin-top: 20px;
        }
        .punchline {
            display: none;
            color: #555;
            font-weight: bold;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="container">
        <h1>My Joke Website</h1>
        <div class="joke">
            <p>[Funny Joke]</p>
            <button onclick="revealPunchline()">Push to reveal punchline</button>
            <p id="punchline" class="punchline">Why don't scientists trust atoms? Because they make up everything!</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <script>
        function revealPunchline() {
            const punchline = document.getElementById('punchline');
            punchline.style.display = 'block';
        }
    </script>
</body>
</html>
```

This HTML and JavaScript code creates a simple, interactive website. It displays a joke and reveals the punchline when the button is clicked. You can replace the text inside the `<p>` tags with any joke you like.
